  "limitations": [
    "GeneratorExit request identities with observed usage are successful completed responses, not failures.",
    "CancelledError alone cannot distinguish first-token deadline, hedge loser, or caller cancellation; 25 failed trials retain no more specific cause.",
    "All 33 APITimeoutError records have ConnectTimeout roots. Only four of eight APIConnectionError records retain proven ConnectError roots; the other four retain unknown billing reservations.",
    "No rate-limit or authentication error is retained. Absence of a retained status is not proof that those errors never occurred.",
    "The last 44 completion-ordered trial records have only two successes versus 152 in the first 160. Temporal failure clustering confounds unblocked architecture comparisons.",
    "118 request reservations are unresolved exposure, not measured spend. Known usage charges are reported separately.",
    "Latency populations are unpaired successful primary answers, including eight trials whose secondary pass failed; these are not speed improvement claims.",
    "first_token_ms measures the winning route opening; first_delta_ms includes engine/router waiting; first_complete_sentence_ms is a sentence boundary, not human-rated usefulness.",
    "Generation-only replay starts from confirmed, preclassified questions with fixed context: STT, detector, production retrieval, UI rendering, and tokenization/provider queue/reasoning stages are not individually measured.",
    "ModelRouter had max_retries=0 in provider SDKs, bounded explicit routes, pooled clients and no retry after streamed text. No evidence supports increasing retries or the existing two-second transport connect default."
